{"agent":"fleet-ciagentenv","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The added autouse fixture `monkeypatch.delenv(\"DDFLOW_AGENT\", raising=False)` makes these tests pass on both the fixed and the unfixed code, so it is not a regression test for B3a8e04ca38 and does not satisfy the project's \"must have regression test\" hard constraint [D-rules-hierarchy]. Concretely: on the unfixed `runner.run_command_gate`, the caller's identity reaches the gate child through `**os.environ`; the test module's fixture deletes `DDFLOW_AGENT` from the pytest process before `run_cli` spawns its subprocess, so the subprocess never receives the variable and `test_clone_id_recovery`'s three cases pass without the runner change being present at all. Because the variable is removed *before* the code under test runs, the new `child_env`/`gates.scrub_env` scrubbing path is never exercised, and the tests cannot fail on unfixed code. A regression test for this bug must instead set `DDFLOW_AGENT` (e.g. via the subprocess environment of `run_cli`), invoke the affected command, and assert the child environment no longer contains it — that assertion fails on the pre-fix code, which is exactly what the fixture suppresses.","digest":"a436add161a8c443","location":"tests/test_clone_id_recovery.py:55 (fixture `_no_caller_identity`)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_clone_id_recovery.py:55 (fixture `_no_caller_identity`)"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":11512,"diff_sha":"8d1a8a818fab413011ef44a6742828f9643d42c55addd065785aea16d6a0bff8","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":303.6,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"ce9e37778a9b04c9","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B3a8e04ca38.critic.lan